    3-8 isolated pixels per rule, each matching that rule's source_color
    placed anywhere on the grid outside the rule-example region
    replaced in output by the stencil translated to center on the pixel, recolored to target_color
    stamps may go out of bounds (clipped) or overlap other stamps
    spurious rule avoidance: scattered src pixels of different src_colors must not form a 4-adjacent pair whose continuation direction reaches a teal cluster, or the solver discovers a false rule
